module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Eval
public import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Rename
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.AffineGlobalBridge
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.CechCoverComplex
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Schemes.ZariskiAndSeparation.IntersectionGeneration

/-!
# The polynomial presentations `P_α → C_α` of the Čech intersections

[Stacks, Tag 07MM] chooses an affine open covering `X = ⋃_λ U_λ = ⋃_λ Spec(C_λ)` and, for each
member, a polynomial algebra `P_λ` over `A = Γ(S, ⊤)` with a surjection `P_λ → C_λ`; out of these
it forms, for every tuple `α = (λ_0, …, λ_n)`, the polynomial algebra

`P_α = P_{λ_0} ⊗_A ⋯ ⊗_A P_{λ_n}`

with its map onto `C_α = Γ(U_α)`, and then the `p`-adically completed divided power envelope `D_α`
of the kernel.

**This file builds the presentations and proves that they are surjective**, which is item 1 of the
"What is and is not proved" list of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/CechCoverComplex.lean`.  No `(n + 1)`-fold
fibre product, and no induction carrying the closed immersion along it, is needed.  The surjectivity
is `...SmallSite.CechPresentation.surjective_tupleMap`, and it is obtained from the *two*-open case
of [Stacks, Tag 01KP] by an induction carried out on the rings of sections rather than on the
schemes — `AlgebraicGeometry.closure_iUnion_range_sectionsRestrict_eq_top`, which says that
`Γ(U_0 ∩ ⋯ ∩ U_n)` is generated by the images of the `Γ(U_j)`.

The envelopes themselves — item 2 of that list — are **still not constructed**, and nothing here
asserts that they are; what this file supplies is exactly the three inputs their universal
property asks for: the surjection, the functoriality of its kernel, and the condition on the
divided power ideal of the base.

## The tensor product is a polynomial algebra, and that is what makes the family functorial

`P_{λ_0} ⊗_A ⋯ ⊗_A P_{λ_n}` is the polynomial algebra over `A` on the *disjoint union* of the
variables of its factors.  Taking that disjoint union as the definition —
`CechPresentation.tupleIndex`, a sigma type — makes the transition maps along the Čech faces
literally `MvPolynomial.rename` of a reindexing of sigma types, and those are *strictly*
functorial: `...CechPresentation.tupleRename_id` and `...CechPresentation.tupleRename_comp` hold
on the nose, with no coherence isomorphisms.  That is what a `...SmallSite.CechSystem`, whose
`map_id` and `map_comp` are equations rather than isomorphisms, will need.

## Main definitions

Everything lives in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`.

* `baseToSections` — the structural map `A = Γ(S, ⊤) → Γ(U)` for an open of `X`.
* `CechPresentation` — **the second choice of [Stacks, Tag 07MM]**: a polynomial algebra `P_λ`
  with a surjection onto `C_λ` for every member of the covering.
* `CechPresentation.tautological` — that choice can always be made, on the variables `C_λ` itself.
* `CechPresentation.tupleIndex`, `CechPresentation.tupleRing` — **the polynomial algebra `P_α`**.
* `CechPresentation.tupleMap` — **the map `P_α → C_α`**.
* `CechPresentation.tupleRename` — **the transition map `P_{α ∘ φ} → P_α`** along a simplex map.
* `CechPresentation.tupleIdeal` — **the ideal `J_α = ker(P_α → C_α)`**, whose `p`-adically
  completed divided power envelope is the ring `D_α` of the remark.
* `CechPresentation.tupleQuotientEquiv` — the identification `P_α / J_α ≅ C_α`.
* `IsCechIntersectionSystem` — that a `...SmallSite.CechSystem` thickens the Čech intersections.

## Main results

* `CechCovering.inter_le_inter_comp` — the Čech intersections are contravariant in the tuple.
* `CechPresentation.tupleRename_id`, `CechPresentation.tupleRename_comp` — the transition maps are
  strictly functorial in the simplex category.
* `CechPresentation.tupleMap_comp_tupleRename` — **the presentations are compatible with the Čech
  faces**: the square relating `P_{α ∘ φ} → P_α` to `C_{α ∘ φ} → C_α` commutes.
* `CechPresentation.surjective_tupleMap` — **the presentation `P_α → C_α` is surjective** for a
  separated `X`.  This is the missing half of item 1.
* `CechPresentation.tupleIdeal_map_le` — **the transition maps carry `J_{α ∘ φ}` into `J_α`**,
  which is the hypothesis under which the universal property of the divided power envelope
  produces the transition morphism `D_{α ∘ φ} ⟶ D_α`.
* `CechPresentation.C_mem_tupleIdeal_of_mem_ideal` — **the divided power ideal `I` of the base
  lies in `J_α`**, the second hypothesis of the envelope.

## What is and is not proved

**Neither [Stacks, Tag 07MM] nor [Stacks, Tag 07MN] is proved here and no tag attribute is placed
in this file.**  The envelopes `D_α` are not constructed; `...SmallSite.CechSystem` and
`...SmallSite.OrdDeRhamSystem` remain carried data and no term of either is built.

Separatedness is used in exactly one place, `CechPresentation.surjective_tupleMap`, through
`AlgebraicGeometry.closure_iUnion_range_sectionsRestrict_eq_top`: the ring `C_α` is generated by
the images of the `C_{λ_j}`, which for two opens is part (1)(b) of [Stacks, Tag 01KP],
`AlgebraicGeometry.sectionTensorMap_surjective_of_isSeparated`.  It is **not an added
hypothesis**: it is the hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 07MM] itself, derived from the remark's
"separated over `S₀`" by `...SmallSite.CechCovering.isSeparated_source`, and the same hypothesis
already carries the affineness of the Čech intersections,
`...SmallSite.CechCovering.isAffineOpen_inter`.  Nor is it removable: for a non-separated `X` the
intersection of two affine opens need not be affine, and the surjection the remark asks for need
not exist.

What stands between this file and the envelopes `D_α` is **not** the presentations and **not** the
universal property of the envelope, which is a genuine `Equiv`
(`Crystalline.DividedPowerEnvelope.homEquiv`) and so determines its lifts uniquely
(`Crystalline.envelopeHom_ext`, `Crystalline.completedEnvelope_hom_ext`).  It is that both live
over a *fixed* `Crystalline.AffineCrystallineSituation`, whose ring `C` is the target of the
presentation: `Crystalline.polynomialEnvelopeMap` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/Cosimplicial/Envelope.lean` maps the envelope of one
presentation of `s.C` to that of another, and `Crystalline.completedEnvelope_isCoproduct`
([Stacks, Tag 07L4]) exhibits `D(n)` as a coproduct of `n + 1` copies of a single `D`, both for
one `s`.  Here the targets `C_α` differ from tuple to tuple, so the affine situations differ, and
there is no map of envelopes across two of them.  Producing the local situation at `U_α` from
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.restrict` is itself unfinished: that construction replaces
the base `S` by `S.S.restrict W`, and for `W = ⊤` nothing identifies `S.S.restrict ⊤` with `S.S`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07L4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07L4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01KP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01KP)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

namespace MvPolynomial

/-- **The image of a ring homomorphism out of a polynomial ring** is the subring generated by the
images of the constants together with the images of the variables. -/
theorem range_eq_closure {R A : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] {σ : Type*}
    (f : MvPolynomial σ R →+* A) :
    f.range = Subring.closure (Set.range (fun r => f (C r)) ∪ Set.range (fun i => f (X i))) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rintro x ⟨p, rfl⟩
    induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
    | C a => exact Subring.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨a, rfl⟩)
    | add p q hp hq => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hp hq
    | mul_X p i hp =>
      rw [map_mul]
      exact mul_mem hp (Subring.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨i, rfl⟩))
  · rw [Subring.closure_le]
    rintro x (⟨a, rfl⟩ | ⟨i, rfl⟩)
    · exact ⟨C a, rfl⟩
    · exact ⟨X i, rfl⟩

/-- **A ring homomorphism out of a polynomial ring is surjective exactly when the images of the
constants and of the variables generate the target.** -/
theorem surjective_iff_closure_eq_top {R A : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] {σ : Type*}
    (f : MvPolynomial σ R →+* A) :
    Function.Surjective f ↔
      Subring.closure (Set.range (fun r => f (C r)) ∪ Set.range (fun i => f (X i))) = ⊤ := by
  rw [← range_eq_closure]
  refine ⟨fun h => eq_top_iff.mpr fun x _ => h x, fun h x => ?_⟩
  have hx : x ∈ f.range := by rw [h]; trivial
  exact hx

end MvPolynomial

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

variable {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} {Λ : Type u}

/-! ### The structural maps from the base -/

/-- **The structural map `A = Γ(S, ⊤) → Γ(U)`** making the sections over an open of `X` an algebra
over the ring `A` of the affine crystalline situation of [Stacks, Tag 07MD].  The type
`Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤)` is the carrier of
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.baseSectionsRing`. -/
abbrev baseToSections (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) (U : S.X.Opens) :
    Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) →+* Γ(S.X, U) :=
  (sectionsRestrict (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)).comp (baseSectionsToSections S)

/-- The structural maps from the base are compatible with restriction. -/
theorem baseToSections_restrict (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) {U V : S.X.Opens}
    (h : V ≤ U) : (sectionsRestrict h).comp (baseToSections S U) = baseToSections S V := by
  ext a
  exact sectionsRestrict_comp (le_top : U ≤ ⊤) h _

/-! ### The Čech intersections are contravariant in the tuple -/

namespace CechCovering

/-- **The Čech intersection of a tuple is contained in the Čech intersection of any reindexing of
it**, the reindexed tuple intersecting a subfamily of the same members.  These are the inclusions
along which the restriction maps of [Stacks, Tag 07MM] are formed. -/
theorem inter_le_inter_comp (c : CechCovering S Λ) {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n)
    (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) :
    c.inter α ≤ c.inter fun i => α (φ.toOrderHom i) :=
  le_iInf fun i => c.inter_le α (φ.toOrderHom i)

end CechCovering

/-! ### The polynomial presentations of the members of the covering -/

/-- **The second of the two choices of [Stacks, Tag 07MM]**: for every member `U_λ = Spec(C_λ)` of
the chosen affine open covering, a polynomial algebra `P_λ` over a base ring `R` together with a
surjection `P_λ → C_λ` of `R`-algebras.

The base ring is left a parameter.  The case of the remark is `R = Γ(S, ⊤) = A` with `base` the
structural maps `baseToSections`; `CechPresentation.C_mem_tupleIdeal_of_mem_ideal` is the one
statement below that fixes it. -/
structure CechPresentation (c : CechCovering S Λ) (R : Type u) [CommRing R] where
  /-- The variables of `P_λ`. -/
  index : Λ → Type u
  /-- The structural map `R → Γ(U)` for every open of `X`. -/
  base : (U : S.X.Opens) → R →+* Γ(S.X, U)
  /-- The structural maps are compatible with restriction. -/
  base_restrict : ∀ {U V : S.X.Opens} (h : V ≤ U), (sectionsRestrict h).comp (base U) = base V
  /-- The chosen presentation `P_λ → C_λ`. -/
  pres : (l : Λ) → MvPolynomial (index l) R →+* Γ(S.X, c.opens l)
  /-- It is a map of `R`-algebras. -/
  pres_C : ∀ (l : Λ) (r : R), pres l (MvPolynomial.C r) = base (c.opens l) r
  /-- It is surjective, which is the remark's "choose a surjection `P_λ → C_λ`". -/
  pres_surjective : ∀ l, Function.Surjective (pres l)

/-- **The choice of [Stacks, Tag 07MM] can always be made**: the tautological presentation, whose
variables are the elements of `C_λ` and which sends `x_a` to `a`.  Its index types live in the
universe of the rings of sections, which is the universe the affine-to-global equivalence of
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.wholeSiteEquivLittleAffine` needs. -/
def CechPresentation.tautological (c : CechCovering S Λ) {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    (base : (U : S.X.Opens) → R →+* Γ(S.X, U))
    (base_restrict : ∀ {U V : S.X.Opens} (h : V ≤ U),
      (sectionsRestrict h).comp (base U) = base V) :
    CechPresentation c R where
  index l := Γ(S.X, c.opens l)
  base := base
  base_restrict := base_restrict
  pres l := MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (base (c.opens l)) id
  pres_C l r := MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C _ _ r
  pres_surjective _ a := ⟨MvPolynomial.X a, by simp⟩

namespace CechPresentation

variable {c : CechCovering S Λ} {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (P : CechPresentation c R)

/-! ### The polynomial algebra `P_α` of a tuple -/

/-- **The variables of `P_α = P_{λ_0} ⊗_R ⋯ ⊗_R P_{λ_n}`**: one copy of the variables of
`P_{λ_j}` for each entry of the tuple.  A tensor product of polynomial algebras over `R` is the
polynomial algebra on the disjoint union of their variables, so this sigma type is the index set of
the tensor product that [Stacks, Tag 07MM] forms. -/
abbrev tupleIndex {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ) : Type u := Σ j, P.index (α j)

/-- **The polynomial algebra `P_α = P_{λ_0} ⊗_R ⋯ ⊗_R P_{λ_n}`** of [Stacks, Tag 07MM]. -/
abbrev tupleRing {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ) : Type u := MvPolynomial (P.tupleIndex α) R

/-- **The map `P_α → C_α`** of [Stacks, Tag 07MM]: on the `j`-th block of variables it is the
chosen presentation of `C_{λ_j}` followed by restriction to the Čech intersection `U_α`. -/
def tupleMap {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ) : P.tupleRing α →+* Γ(S.X, c.inter α) :=
  MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (P.base (c.inter α))
    fun x => sectionsRestrict (c.inter_le α x.1) (P.pres (α x.1) (MvPolynomial.X x.2))

/-- The map `P_α → C_α` sends a constant `r` to the image of `r` in `C_α`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tupleMap_C {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ) (r : R) :
    P.tupleMap α (MvPolynomial.C r) = P.base (c.inter α) r :=
  MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C _ _ r

/-- The map `P_α → C_α` sends the variable `x` of the `j`-th block to the restriction to `U_α` of
its image under the chosen presentation of `C_{λ_j}`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tupleMap_X {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ) (x : P.tupleIndex α) :
    P.tupleMap α (MvPolynomial.X x) =
      sectionsRestrict (c.inter_le α x.1) (P.pres (α x.1) (MvPolynomial.X x.2)) :=
  MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X' _ _ x

/-! ### The transition maps along the Čech faces -/

/-- **Reindexing the variables of `P_α` along a simplex map**: the `i`-th block of variables of
`P_{α ∘ φ}` is the `φ(i)`-th block of variables of `P_α`.  This is the inclusion of tensor factors
`P_{α ∘ φ} → P_α`, read on variables, and it is *strictly* functorial. -/
def tupleIndexMap {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n) (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) :
    P.tupleIndex (fun i => α (φ.toOrderHom i)) → P.tupleIndex α :=
  fun x => ⟨φ.toOrderHom x.1, x.2⟩

/-- **The transition map `P_{α ∘ φ} → P_α`** of [Stacks, Tag 07MM], the inclusion of tensor
factors along a simplex map. -/
def tupleRename {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n) (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) :
    P.tupleRing (fun i => α (φ.toOrderHom i)) →+* P.tupleRing α :=
  (MvPolynomial.rename (P.tupleIndexMap φ α)).toRingHom

/-- The transition map `P_{α ∘ φ} → P_α` fixes constants. -/
@[simp]
theorem tupleRename_C {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n) (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) (r : R) :
    P.tupleRename φ α (MvPolynomial.C r) = MvPolynomial.C r :=
  MvPolynomial.rename_C _ r

/-- The transition map `P_{α ∘ φ} → P_α` sends a variable `x` to the variable
`tupleIndexMap φ α x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tupleRename_X {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n) (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ)
    (x : P.tupleIndex fun i => α (φ.toOrderHom i)) :
    P.tupleRename φ α (MvPolynomial.X x) = MvPolynomial.X (P.tupleIndexMap φ α x) :=
  MvPolynomial.rename_X _ x

/-- **The transition map along an identity is an identity.** -/
theorem tupleRename_id (n : SimplexCategory) (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) :
    P.tupleRename (𝟙 n) α = RingHom.id (P.tupleRing α) :=
  RingHom.ext fun p => MvPolynomial.rename_id_apply (R := R) (σ := P.tupleIndex α) p

/-- **The transition maps compose**, contravariantly in the simplex category. -/
theorem tupleRename_comp {l m n : SimplexCategory} (ψ : l ⟶ m) (φ : m ⟶ n)
    (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) :
    P.tupleRename (ψ ≫ φ) α =
      (P.tupleRename φ α).comp (P.tupleRename ψ fun j => α (φ.toOrderHom j)) :=
  RingHom.ext fun p =>
    (MvPolynomial.rename_rename (P.tupleIndexMap ψ fun j => α (φ.toOrderHom j))
      (P.tupleIndexMap φ α) p).symm

/-- The structural maps of a presentation commute with restriction, elementwise. -/
private theorem sectionsRestrict_base (U V : S.X.Opens) (h : V ≤ U) (r : R) :
    sectionsRestrict h (P.base U r) = P.base V r :=
  RingHom.congr_fun (P.base_restrict h) r

/-- **The presentations of the Čech intersections are compatible with the Čech faces**: the
transition map `P_{α ∘ φ} → P_α` followed by `P_α → C_α` is `P_{α ∘ φ} → C_{α ∘ φ}` followed by
restriction along the inclusion `U_α ⊆ U_{α ∘ φ}`.

This is the commuting square of presentations which, together with
`CechPresentation.tupleIdeal_map_le`, is what the universal property of the divided power envelope
takes as input. -/
theorem tupleMap_comp_tupleRename {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n)
    (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) :
    (P.tupleMap α).comp (P.tupleRename φ α) =
      (sectionsRestrict (c.inter_le_inter_comp φ α)).comp
        (P.tupleMap fun i => α (φ.toOrderHom i)) := by
  refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun r => ?_) fun x => ?_
  · simp [sectionsRestrict_base]
  · change P.tupleMap α (P.tupleRename φ α (MvPolynomial.X x)) =
      sectionsRestrict (c.inter_le_inter_comp φ α)
        (P.tupleMap (fun i => α (φ.toOrderHom i)) (MvPolynomial.X x))
    rw [tupleRename_X, tupleMap_X, tupleMap_X, sectionsRestrict_comp]
    rfl

/-! ### Surjectivity of the presentations -/

/-- **The presentation `P_α → C_α` of a Čech intersection is surjective**, for a separated `X`.

This is the half of item 1 of the "What is and is not proved" list of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/CechCoverComplex.lean` that was missing, and
it is where the separatedness hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 07MM] is used a second time — the first
being the affineness of the Čech intersections,
`...SmallSite.CechCovering.isAffineOpen_inter`.

The geometric input is `AlgebraicGeometry.closure_iUnion_range_sectionsRestrict_eq_top`: the ring
`C_α` is generated by the images of the `C_{λ_j}`, which for two opens is part (1)(b) of
[Stacks, Tag 01KP].  Given that, surjectivity is formal: the image of `P_α` is the subring
generated by the image of `R` together with the images of the variables, and the image of the
`j`-th block of variables generates the image of `C_{λ_j}` because `P_{λ_j} → C_{λ_j}` is onto. -/
theorem surjective_tupleMap [Scheme.IsSeparated S.X] {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ) :
    Function.Surjective (P.tupleMap α) := by
  rw [MvPolynomial.surjective_iff_closure_eq_top]
  have hgeo := closure_iUnion_range_sectionsRestrict_eq_top (X := S.X) n
    (fun j => c.opens (α j)) (fun j => c.isAffineOpen_opens (α j)) (c.inter α) rfl
    (fun j => c.inter_le α j)
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr ?_
  rw [← hgeo, Subring.closure_le]
  rintro z hz
  obtain ⟨j, y, rfl⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.mp hz
  obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := P.pres_surjective (α j) y
  rw [SetLike.mem_coe]
  have hq : sectionsRestrict (c.inter_le α j) (P.pres (α j) q) ∈
      ((sectionsRestrict (c.inter_le α j)).comp (P.pres (α j))).range := ⟨q, rfl⟩
  rw [MvPolynomial.range_eq_closure] at hq
  refine Subring.closure_le.mpr ?_ hq
  rintro w (⟨r, rfl⟩ | ⟨i, rfl⟩)
  · exact SetLike.mem_coe.mpr (Subring.subset_closure
      (Or.inl ⟨r, by simp [P.pres_C, sectionsRestrict_base]⟩))
  · exact SetLike.mem_coe.mpr
      (Subring.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨⟨j, i⟩, P.tupleMap_X α ⟨j, i⟩⟩))

/-! ### The ideals whose divided power envelopes are the `D_α` -/

/-- **The ideal `J_α = ker(P_α → C_α)`** whose `p`-adically completed divided power envelope is the
ring `D_α` of [Stacks, Tag 07MM]. -/
def tupleIdeal {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ) : Ideal (P.tupleRing α) :=
  RingHom.ker (P.tupleMap α)

/-- **`C_α` is the quotient `P_α / J_α`**, for a separated `X`.

This is the presentation of [Stacks, Tag 07MM] in the form its divided power envelope uses it: the
envelope of `J_α` has `P_α / J_α` as the quotient by its divided power ideal, and that quotient
must be `C_α` for the envelope to be an object of a crystalline site over `C_α`. -/
def tupleQuotientEquiv [Scheme.IsSeparated S.X] {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ) :
    (P.tupleRing α ⧸ P.tupleIdeal α) ≃+* Γ(S.X, c.inter α) :=
  RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (P.surjective_tupleMap α)

/-- **The transition maps carry `J_{α ∘ φ}` into `J_α`.**

This is the hypothesis under which the universal property of the divided power envelope,
`Crystalline.DividedPowerEnvelope.homEquiv`, produces the transition morphism `D_{α ∘ φ} ⟶ D_α` of
the system of [Stacks, Tag 07MM].  It is the Čech-indexed replacement for the coprojections
`D ⟶ D(n)` of [Stacks, Tag 07L4], `Crystalline.completedEnvelopeCoprojection`, which exist only
for the tensor powers of a single presentation. -/
theorem tupleIdeal_map_le {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n) (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) :
    (P.tupleIdeal fun i => α (φ.toOrderHom i)).map (P.tupleRename φ α) ≤ P.tupleIdeal α := by
  rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  intro q hq
  rw [tupleIdeal, RingHom.mem_ker] at hq
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, tupleIdeal, RingHom.mem_ker]
  have h := RingHom.congr_fun (P.tupleMap_comp_tupleRename φ α) q
  simp only [RingHom.comp_apply] at h
  rw [h, hq, map_zero]

end CechPresentation

section BaseIdeal

variable {c : CechCovering S Λ}

/-- **The divided power ideal `I` of the base lies in `J_α`.**

The structure morphism `X ⟶ S` factors through the closed fibre `S₀ = V(I)`, so `I` has zero image
in `Γ(X, ⊤)` and hence in every `C_α`.  This is the hypothesis `I · P_α ⊆ J_α` under which the
divided power envelope of `J_α` relative to the base `(A, I, γ)` is formed — the argument `hJ` of
`Crystalline.dividedPowerEnvelope`. -/
theorem CechPresentation.C_mem_tupleIdeal_of_mem_ideal
    (P : CechPresentation c Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤))
    (hP : ∀ U : S.X.Opens, P.base U = baseToSections S U) {n : ℕ} (α : Fin (n + 1) → Λ)
    (r : Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤)) (hr : r ∈ S.S.ideal.obj (op ⊤)) :
    MvPolynomial.C r ∈ P.tupleIdeal α := by
  rw [CechPresentation.tupleIdeal, RingHom.mem_ker, CechPresentation.tupleMap_C, hP]
  change sectionsRestrict (le_top : c.inter α ≤ ⊤) (baseSectionsToSections S r) = 0
  rw [baseSectionsToSections_eq_zero_of_mem S r hr, map_zero]

end BaseIdeal

/-! ### What the envelopes `D_α` still owe -/

/-- **A Čech system of thickenings of the Čech intersections**: the open of `X` that `T(α)_e`
thickens is `U_α`.

In [Stacks, Tag 07MM] this holds by construction, `T(α)_e = Spec(D_α/p^e D_α)` being a thickening
of `U_α = Spec(C_α)`.  It is the only part of the description of that system which can be stated
without the envelopes themselves: the identification of the ring of `T(α)_e` with a level of the
completed divided power envelope of `CechPresentation.tupleIdeal` cannot be written down here,
there being no `Crystalline.AffineCrystallineSituation` at `U_α` for the envelope to be taken in.

**This predicate is not asserted of any system**, and it is emphatically not the statement of
[Stacks, Tag 07MM]: no term of `...SmallSite.CechSystem` is constructed anywhere in this
library. -/
def IsCechIntersectionSystem (c : CechCovering S Λ) (T : CechSystem S Λ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (n : SimplexCategory) (α : Fin (n.len + 1) → Λ) (e : ℕ),
    Set.range ((T.obj n α).obj e).obj.toX.base = (c.inter α : Set S.X)

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

end
